In a standard 52‑card deck, the probability of being dealt a full house in a 5‑card hand is:

\[
P(\text{full house}) = \frac{13 \times \binom{4}{3} \times 12 \times \binom{4}{2}}{\binom{52}{5}}
                     = \frac{3744}{2\,598\,960}
                     \approx 0.00144 \;\text{(about 0.144 %)}.
\]
